-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Windows EC2 
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Create New User in Windows EC2:
Create a Windows EC2 instance.
Login to Windows EC2 using RDP
 Press Windows + R
 Type -> lusrmgr.msc
 Click OK
Local Users and Groups window opens
Click -> Users
Right click inside empty area
Select -> New User
Enter:
Username
Password
Confirm Password
Optional:
Uncheck -> User must change password at next logon
Check -> Password never expires
Click -> Create
Click -> Close
Double click created user
Open -> Member Of tab
Click -> Add
Enter: Administrators
Click -> Check Names
Click -> OK
Click -> Apply
Click -> OK

Login Using Created User:
Close current RDP session
Press Windows + R
Type -> mstsc
Press Enter
Paste Public IP/Public DNS
Click Connect
More Choices:
Username ->Created username
Enter password
Click OK
Windows desktop opens using new user

See Hostname in Windows EC2
Login to Windows EC2 using RDP
Press Windows + R
Type ->cmd
Press Enter
Command Prompt opens
Type:
hostname
Press Enter
Current hostname/computer name will be displayed

Change Hostname in Windows EC2:
Press Windows + R
Type -> sysdm.cpl
Press Enter
Open -> Computer Name tab
Click -> Change
Enter new computer name
Example:
Windows-Server
Click OK
Restart system
Hostname changes successfully

Website Hosting:
Instance created
Select windows instance
Open Security Tab {Below the instance details: Security}
Click Edit inbound rules
Add rules 
RDP (if not there); HTTP
{Type: HTTP; port:80; source: anywhere}
Save rules
Connect with your windows EC2 instance 
Inside that
1) Click: Server Manager
2) Click: Add roles and features
3) Select: At top right-> Manage: Role-based or feature-based installation
4) Click: Next
5) Click: Next
6) Check: Web Server (IIS)
7) Click: Add Features
8) Click: Next (until install page comes)
9) Click: Install
10)Click: Close
11) Open File Explorer
12) Go to: C:\inetpub\wwwroot
13) View → Show → File name extensions->Right-click blank space: New → Text Document
14) Rename file: index.html
15) Click: Yes {if file extension warning appears}
17) Open: index.html
18) Type: <h1>Hello from Windows EC2 Website</h1>
19) Save file
20) Copy: index.html
21) Paste into: C:\inetpub\wwwroot
22) Go back to EC2 Console (minimize button or alt+tab)
23) Copy: Public IPv4 address
24) Open browser
25) Type: http://PUBLIC-IP
26) Press Enter
27) Webpage opens successfully


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Linux EC2
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
See Hostname in Linux EC2:
Connect to Linux EC2 terminal
Type: hostname
Press Enter
Current hostname will be displayed

Change Hostname in Linux EC2:
Connect to Linux EC2 terminal
Type:
sudo hostnamectl set-hostname Linux-Server
Press Enter
Hostname changes
Verify:
hostname

Create New User in Linux EC2:
Connect to Linux EC2 terminal
Create user:
sudo adduser student
Set password:
sudo passwd student
Enter new password
Re-enter password

Give Admin/Sudo Access to User:
Type:
sudo usermod -aG wheel student

Switch to that user:
su - student

Login Using Created User:
Connect to Linux EC2 terminal
Initially user 
su – student
Enter password
Changed to student from user.

Website Hosting:
Instance created
Select Linux Instance
Open Security Tab {Below the instance details: Security}
Under: Security groups Click the security group link.
Click Edit inbound rules
Click Add rule: SSH (if not there); HTTP
{Type: HTTP; port:80; source: anywhere}
Save rules
Select Linux instance->connect->Ec2 Instance connect-> connect
Inside Terminal
1) sudo su
2) yum install httpd -y
3) systemctl start httpd
4) systemctl enable httpd
5) cd /var/www/html {go to default website folder of apache web server}
6) mkdir website {create folder name: website}
7) cd website {open folder website}
8) touch index.html {create file index.html}
9) echo "<h1>Hello from Linux EC2 Website</h1>" > index.html {write into file}
10) cat index.html {Read file}
11) cp index.html /var/www/html {Copy index.html file to Apache main website folder}
Go back to EC2 console
Copy public IPV4 address
Open new tab copy, paste, enter
The webpage opens
